  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Regional Advisory Group will meet in Maputo, from September 30 to October 04, and will consist of 2 days of field visit and 3 days of workshop.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Regional Advisory group meets in a yearly base, and this is composed of all the implementing partners of the Regional Programme on SRHR and HIV/AIDS, namely: Aidsfonds, Frontline Aids, IOM, UNFPA, UNDP and Young Africa representatives.
Besides the regular members, also we will have the participation of guests from DSO-GS from the Hague, members of Youth Networks of people living with HIV (Y+) and local partners.

For this year the RAG will take place in Maputo, Mozambique and it is schedule to have filed visits to Maputo Province and the 3 days of workshop in Radisson.

This year, besides the regular discussions on how to improve the programme, also there will be the presentation of the preliminary results of the Mid Term Review. This will be a unique opportunity to reflect on the past and present and make commitments for the future of the Regional Programme on SRHR and HIV/Aids.</narrative>
  </description>
